  "description": "A parametric BAFFLE CEILING on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nDROP IT ON A SPACE. The blades run along the space's longest edge (Rotation turns them) and fill its bounding box less the inset. Use a rectangular ceiling-zone space for an angled room: the field is the host's box, not its outline.\n\nWAVE = THE BOTTOM EDGE, NOT THE BLADE. Each blade is cut into segments of Wave segment length; a segment's bottom sits at bottomLevel + A·(½ + ½·sin(2πu/λ + i·φ)), so the lowest edge is exactly bottomLevel and the wave travels across the field by φ per blade. The tops stay level at bottomLevel + A + height — a hung baffle has a straight top.\n\nCOLOUR is by row: Alternate puts odd blades on the Baffles B row, so two felt colours need no second object. END PROFILE caps the blade ends with a straight band (the deck's review: white, rectangular, need not follow the wave — slides 23, 27); Full frame also runs it down the long sides, which hides the wave from the side.\n\nDEFAULTS are the INFRA Reception spec: 25 mm blades, 150 mm deep, 50 mm clear, lowest edge 2700 FFL.",
